    pure_sql_reopen_checkpointed_file_stack_overflow_2026-08-25, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: doc sequence (open_deferred, CREATE TABLE, INSERT, checkpoint, second open_deferred same file, two processes) passes on both default JIT and interpreter lanes with the v3 envelope shape the doc isolated as trigger. Root cause per the doc addenda was never recursion: the seed JIT boxed parse_int/parse_f64 tagged returns into Some(nil) so _load_from_disk rejected intact images; every function in the re-open path is already iterative (_load_from_disk pure_database.spl:1480, _deserialize_row_v2, _pdb_v3_row_encoding_is_canonical - all while loops). Both fixes are ancestors of HEAD: 72a04293111 (_pdb_decimal_parse_strict + strict canonicality + the regression spec) and a3f4f27a7ff (seed register_optional boxing). Verification matrix on fresh HEAD seed: pure_sql_reopen_checkpointed_spec 1/1, select_cache 10/10, autoincrement 2/2, reopen_multibyte 2/2, numeric_parse_contract 6/6, test/02_integration/app/pure_sql_reopen_process_spec 4/4 on the JIT lane. Pre-existing unrelated failures (pure_sql_query_debug_v1; schema_v3 two failures incl unknown-type-name-maps-to-TEXT committed parser/spec mismatch) left for their owners. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/database/pure_sql_reopen_checkpointed_spec.spl prevention=test/02_integration/app/pure_sql_reopen_process_spec.spl"

